<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/17th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty</p><h1 class="enc-title">Treaty of Stettin (1653)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1653">1653</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Treaty of Stettin of May 1653 between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brandenburg">Brandenburg</a> fixed the border in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pomerania">Pomerania</a> after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peace-of-westphalia">Peace of Westphalia</a> had divided the former duchy. Sweden kept Western Pomerania with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/szczecin">Stettin</a> and the mouth of the Oder, while Brandenburg finally took over <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/further-pomerania">Farther Pomerania</a>, which Swedish troops had continued to occupy.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/treaty-of-stettin-1653.jpg" alt="Treaty of Stettin (1653)" width="320" height="195" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Astrokey44, section cut by Skäpperöd · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pomerania_1653.PNG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
